# Free Deployment Strategy — Udemy Course Finder

## Your Stack (4 services)

| Component | Tech | What It Does |
|-----------|------|-------------|
| **Frontend** | Next.js 16, Tailwind, Radix UI | Dashboard UI |
| **Backend** | NestJS 11, Prisma, BullMQ | API + job orchestration |
| **Scraper** | Python, BeautifulSoup, Redis queue | Scrapes Udemy courses |
| **Data** | PostgreSQL (pgvector) + Redis | Storage + job queue |

---

## The Simplest Free Deploy

### 1. Frontend → [Vercel](https://vercel.com) (free tier)

**Why**: It's Next.js. Vercel built Next.js. Zero config.

- Connect your GitHub repo
- Set root directory to `frontend/`
- Add env var: `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://your-backend.onrender.com`
- Done. Auto-deploys on push.

**Free tier gives you**: Unlimited deploys, edge CDN, preview URLs per PR, 100 GB bandwidth/mo.

---

### 2. Backend + Scraper → [Render](https://render.com) (free tier)

**Why**: Supports Docker natively, free PostgreSQL, free Redis — all your infra in one place.

#### Backend (Web Service)
- New → Web Service → connect repo
- Root directory: `backend/`
- Build: `npm ci && npx prisma generate && npm run build`
- Start: `npm run start:prod`
- Add env vars (DATABASE_URL, REDIS_URL, JWT secrets, etc.)

#### Scraper (Background Worker)
- New → Background Worker → connect repo
- Root directory: `scraper/`
- Build: `pip install -r requirements.txt`
- Start: `python run_all.py`
- Add env vars (DATABASE_URL, REDIS_URL, SCRAPE_INTERVAL_MINUTES, etc.)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Render free tier services **spin down after 15 min of inactivity** and take ~30-50s to cold start. This is fine for the scraper (it runs on a schedule anyway) and acceptable for a side project backend.

---

### 3. PostgreSQL → [Render](https://render.com) (free tier) or [Neon](https://neon.tech) (free tier)

| | Render Postgres | Neon Postgres |
|--|----------------|---------------|
| Storage | 1 GB | 0.5 GB |
| Expiry | 90 days then deleted | No expiry |
| pgvector | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes |
| Sleep | No | Auto-scales to zero |

> [!TIP]
> **Recommendation: Neon**. No 90-day deletion. pgvector supported. Generous free tier (0.5 GB storage, 190 compute hours/mo). Set your `DATABASE_URL` to the Neon connection string.

---

### 4. Redis → [Upstash](https://upstash.com) (free tier)

**Why**: Only free serverless Redis that doesn't expire.

- 10,000 commands/day free
- 256 MB storage
- REST + standard Redis protocol
- Perfect for BullMQ job queues at low volume

Set `REDIS_URL=rediss://default:xxx@xxx.upstash.io:6379`

> [!NOTE]
> BullMQ works with Upstash Redis. Use the standard `redis://` connection URL (Upstash provides it). The 10K commands/day limit is plenty for a scraper that runs a few times daily.

